{"parentUuid":"3aef28f6-912d-4489-9141-da5f2ed22536","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0c7a1291-4893-4b10-ab88-19df8f6fc7be","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"1. High: Pi is only registered on the `hooks` command path, not on the normal CLI startup path, so the new agent will be invisible to ordinary commands like `entire agent list`, `entire agent add pi`, `attach --agent pi`, and any `agent.Get/List` call outside `hooks`. `hooks_cmd.go` imports the package for registration ([hooks_cmd.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/hooks_cmd.go:11)), but the shared CLI registration site still imports only Claude/Codex/Droid ([config.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/config.go:13)). Since Pi has no other non-test runtime import, its `init()` never runs for the main CLI path.\n\n2. High: `attach`/rewind resolution for Pi only looks in `.entire/tmp`, which means uncaptured or cold Pi sessions are not attachable at all. `resolveAndValidateTranscript` relies on the agent’s `GetSessionDir`/`ResolveSessionFile` to find a session ([attach.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/attach.go:641)), but Pi points that lookup at the repo-local cache rather than Pi’s native session store ([pi.go](/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/pi.go:66)). That cache only exists after hooks have already copied a transcript, so the documented recovery case for `attach` (“hooks failed / weren’t installed”) won’t work for Pi.\n\nPi package tests pass (`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi`). I wasn’t able to run the broader `./cmd/entire/cli` test slice in this environment because module resolution failed against the temporary `GOMODCACHE`, so there’s still a coverage gap around the normal CLI registration path."},"uuid":"3c272b0a-4629-4357-a705-478f316be8a0","timestamp":"2026-05-09T20:14:04.076Z","permissionMode":"acceptEdits","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId"