{"parentUuid":"2b4103d2-84ac-4659-a017-37b9622817c7","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01MqUrVmXoeV6PSa2QxygW25","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"## Response to the review\n\n**Issue 1 (registration):** Empirically a non-issue. `hooks_cmd.go` is a regular file in the `cli` package, so its blank imports run `init()` for every CLI invocation, not only when `entire hooks <…>` is dispatched. I confirmed by running `entire agent list` from a vanilla repo with the production binary — pi shows up. The same applies to copilot-cli, cursor, gemini, opencode, and vogon, which are *only* blank-imported in `hooks_cmd.go` and all appear in `agent list`. Go doesn't gate per-file init by which command path is taken; if the package is imported anywhere, every `init()` in every file runs.\n\nThat said, the split between `config.go` (3 agents) and `hooks_cmd.go` (9 agents, redundant for the 3) reads as drift, and pi sitting only on the \"newer\" side did make the registration look conditional at a glance. I added pi to `config.go` too — defensive duplication, not a fix. Commit: `d47c2d7c4`.\n\n**Issue 2 (cold attach):** Real and worth fixing — thanks. Pi inherited a `GetSessionDir` that pointed at `.entire/tmp` (the per-repo cache, only populated after `agent_end` copies the live JSONL there). That meant cold sessions or sessions where hook capture failed couldn't be resolved by `entire attach`. Fixed: `GetSessionDir` now returns Pi's native store at `<piHome>/sessions/<encoded-repo-path>/`, with the encoded path matching Pi's own scheme. `ResolveSessionFile` globs `*_<id>.jsonl` and returns the most recent timestamp match. Added `GetSessionBaseDir` so the cross-project fallback in `searchTranscriptInProjectDirs` works. The `.entire/tmp` cache stays as a hook-internal detail. Honors `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` and adds `ENTIRE_TEST_PI_SESSION_DIR`. Commit: `a68586ba6`.\n\n**Verified:**\n- 9 new unit tests for encoding, glob lookup, env overrides, and `SessionBaseDirProvider` (`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/`)\n- Cold-attach integration check: created a Pi session with no Entire hooks installed, ran `entire session attach --agent pi <id>`, it resolved the live JSONL in pi's native store, parsed token usage (1055 in / 11 out / 1 API call), and produced a valid checkpoint trailer\n- E2E canary `TestSingleSessionManualCommit/pi` still passes (7.46s) — the hooked flow is unaffected\n- `mise run lint` clean\n- `cmd/entire/cli`, `cmd/entire/cli/agent`, `cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi`, `cmd/entire/cli/summarize` all `ok`\n\n**Known follow-up (out of scope):** Pi doesn't implement `RestoredSessionPathResolver`, so resume-style restored transcripts are written without the `<timestamp>_` prefix Pi expects in its filename. This was equally broken before the move (cache path was `.entire/tmp/<id>.json` which Pi also wouldn't recognize) and isn't part of the cold-attach scenario the reviewer raised, so I left it for a separate change."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":327,"cache_read_input_tokens":360715,"output_tokens":1151,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":327,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1151,"cache_read_input_tokens":360715,"cache_creation_input_tokens":327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":327},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CasfocYaqMSD7e5UbxJhA","type":"assistant","uuid":"5d4e1ff8-7e47-47f4-9625-bb76586e30a9","timestamp":"2026-05-09T21:02:00.190Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"824c9ef4-e4d5-49d7-ad05-c34c07511466","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"soph/move-pi-in"}
