{"parentUuid":"f478b660-3924-48e6-956e-d08a8ca67dbb","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01C7WKPPt2P4Kwt1Xy6cH6sz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Confirmed: `copilotcli/transcript.go` uses 10 MB and `claudecode/reviewer.go` uses 16 MB. My 1 MB buffer in pi/transcript.go is below the codebase norm and would silently truncate Pi sessions where a tool call embeds a large file's contents in its arguments. PR #1170 fixed this in their review-feedback pass.\n\n## Bottom line\n\n**PR #1170 is the better port.** Eight independent improvements over a straight copy of the external plugin (foreign-file safety, marker-based ownership, repo-local DetectPresence, `--session <id>` resume, `.entire/tmp/pi/` namespacing, SessionEnd on shutdown, current NPM scope, shared `pijsonl/` package). The architecture also slots correctly into the framework: compact lives in `transcript/compact/` like other agents, parsing is shared so divergence can't happen, `localDev` works.\n\n**My port had two real wins they didn't:**\n1. Cold-attach support — `GetSessionDir` points at Pi's native store with glob-by-id resolution and a cross-project fallback. Theirs still hits the cache, so a session that wasn't hooked is unattachable. (This was the reviewer's issue 2 from the earlier round; PR #1170's authors apparently didn't see that case.)\n2. E2E registration + docs.\n\n**Three things mine does worse and should be fixed if mine is the basis going forward:**\n1. `localDev` flag is dropped on the floor — local development against an unbuilt CLI doesn't work\n2. 1 MB scanner buffer truncates large tool-call args; should be 10 MB\n3. `session_shutdown` doesn't emit `SessionEnd`, so the lifecycle state machine never sees the session terminate\n4. Plus the smaller items: foreign-file overwrite, PATH-based DetectPresence, always-`--continue` resume, `.entire/tmp` collision risk\n\n**My recommendation:** if PR #1170 hasn't merged yet, push my cold-attach fix into it (or open a follow-up) — that's the one capability worth carrying over. Mine's other deltas (E2E, docs) port over trivially. The framework integration in PR #1170 is the better foundation; I'd not maintain mine in parallel."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":558,"cache_read_input_tokens":392359,"output_tokens":985,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":558,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":985,"cache_read_input_tokens":392359,"cache_creation_input_tokens":558,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":558},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CashGg2Yh9d4nyHnFL1oY","type":"assistant","uuid":"884da870-df89-4e6a-8ce1-0292e17f3034","timestamp":"2026-05-09T21:21:14.873Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"824c9ef4-e4d5-49d7-ad05-c34c07511466","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"soph/move-pi-in"}
