{"parentUuid":"4a274690-bcc6-466b-93a1-c904b620668c","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/pi.go","snippet":"1\t// Package pi implements the Agent interface for the pi coding agent\n2\t// (https://github.com/earendil-works/pi-mono).\n3\t// The npm package the embedded extension imports a type from is\n4\t// `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent`.\n5\t//\n6\t// This is an in-tree port of the previously-external entire-agent-pi plugin\n7\t// (github.com/entireio/external-agents/agents/entire-agent-pi). The behaviour\n8\t// matches the external version — most notably the active-branch resolution\n9\t// for Pi's tree-shaped sessions — but the integration is plumbed directly\n10\t// through the in-tree Agent / HookSupport / TokenCalculator / TranscriptAnalyzer\n11\t// interfaces rather than the external JSON-over-stdio protocol.\n12\tpackage pi\n13\t\n14\timport (\n15\t\t\"context\"\n16\t\t\"errors\"\n17\t\t\"fmt\"\n18\t\t\"log/slog\"\n19\t\t\"os\"\n20\t\t\"path/filepath\"\n21\t\t\"strings\"\n22\t\n23\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent\"\n24\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/types\"\n25\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/logging\"\n26\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/paths\"\n27\t)\n28\t\n29\t//nolint:gochecknoinits // Agent self-registration is the intended pattern\n30\tfunc init() {\n31\t\tagent.Register(agent.AgentNamePi, NewPiAgent)\n32\t}\n33\t\n34\t// PiAgent implements agent.Agent for the pi coding agent.\n35\t//\n36\t//nolint:revive // PiAgent is clearer than Agent in this context\n37\ttype PiAgent struct{}\n38\t\n39\t// NewPiAgent returns a new Pi agent instance.\n40\tfunc NewPiAgent() agent.Agent {\n41\t\treturn &PiAgent{}\n42\t}\n43\t\n44\t// --- Identity ---\n45\t\n46\tfunc (a *PiAgent) Name() types.AgentName    { return agent.AgentNamePi }\n47\tfunc (a *PiAgent) Type() types.AgentType    { return agent.AgentTypePi }\n48\tfunc (a *PiAgent) Description() string      { return \"Pi coding agent integration for Entire\" }\n49\tfunc (a *PiAgent) IsPreview() bool          { return true }\n50\tfunc (a *PiAgent) ProtectedDirs() []string  { return []string{\".pi\"} }\n51\tfunc (a *PiAgent) ProtectedFiles() []string { return nil }\n52\t\n53\t// DetectPresence reports whether pi is configured for *this repo*. We only\n54\t// check repo-local config (.pi/) and intentionally ignore $PATH — in-tree\n55\t// agents follow the convention used by Claude/Gemini/OpenCode where\n56\t// detection means \"this repo is set up for this agent\", not \"this agent is\n57\t// installed somewhere on this machine\". The external plugin uses the broader\n58\t// $PATH check because it can't see repo state; we don't have that limitation.\n59\tfunc (a *PiAgent) DetectPresence(ctx context.Context) (bool, error) {\n60\t\trepoRoot, err := paths.WorktreeRoot(ctx)\n61\t\tif err != nil {\n62\t\t\trepoRoot = \".\"\n63\t\t}\n64\t\tif _, err := os.Stat(filepath.Join(repoRoot, \".pi\")); err == nil {\n65\t\t\treturn true, nil\n66\t\t}\n67\t\treturn false, nil\n68\t}\n69\t\n70\t// --- Transcript Storage (chunking) ---\n71\t\n72\t// ReadTranscript reads a captured Pi JSONL session transcript from disk.\n73\t// SessionRef is the absolute path returned by captureTranscript().\n74\tfunc (a *PiAgent) ReadTranscript(sessionRef string) ([]byte, error) {\n75\t\tif sessionRef == \"\" {\n76\t\t\treturn nil, errors.New(\"empty session ref\")\n77\t\t}\n78\t\t//nolint:gosec // SessionRef from validated lifecycle hook input\n79\t\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(sessionRef)\n80\t\tif err != nil {\n81\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"read pi transcript %s: %w\", sessionRef, err)\n82\t\t}\n83\t\treturn data, nil\n84\t}\n85\t\n86\t// ChunkTranscript splits a Pi JSONL transcript at line boundaries.\n87\tfunc (a *PiAgent) ChunkTranscript(_ context.Context, content []byte, maxSize int) ([][]byte, error) {\n88\t\tchunks, err := agent.ChunkJSONL(content, maxSize)\n89\t\tif err != nil {\n90\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"chunk pi transcript: %w\", err)\n91\t\t}\n92\t\treturn chunks, nil\n93\t}\n94\t\n95\t// ReassembleTranscript concatenates JSONL chunks with newlines.\n96\tfunc (a *PiAgent) ReassembleTranscript(chunks [][]byte) ([]byte, error) {\n97\t\treturn agent.ReassembleJSONL(chunks), nil\n98\t}\n99\t\n100\t// --- Legacy methods ---\n101\t\n102\t// GetSessionID extracts the session ID from a hook input.\n103\tfunc (a *PiAgent) GetSessionID(input *agent.HookInput) string {\n104\t\tif input == nil {\n105\t\t\treturn \"\"\n106\t\t}\n107\t\treturn input.SessionID\n108\t}\n109\t\n110\t// piSessionSubdir is the per-agent subdirectory under .entire/tmp/ where\n111\t// Pi captures session transcripts. This MUST be agent-specific (not just\n112\t// .entire/tmp) — the framework's AgentForTranscriptPath iterates every\n113\t// agent's session dir to identify the owner of a transcript path, and a\n114\t// broader claim would shadow the .entire/tmp/ paths used by other agents'\n115\t// integration tests and tooling.\n116\tconst piSessionSubdir = \"pi\"\n117\t\n118\t// GetSessionDir returns the directory where Entire stages Pi session\n119\t// transcripts. The Pi extension forwards Pi's native JSONL path on every\n120\t// hook event; on agent_end we copy the file into\n121\t// <repo>/.entire/tmp/pi/<id>.json so condensation can find it\n122\t// deterministically and survive Pi sessions being deleted by the user.\n123\t//\n124\t// When repoPath is empty we resolve the worktree root (so callers running\n125\t// from a subdirectory still get the repo-local staging path) and only fall\n126\t// back to os.Getwd() if no git repo is reachable.\n127\tfunc (a *PiAgent) GetSessionDir(repoPath string) (string, error) {\n128\t\tif repoPath == \"\" {\n129\t\t\troot, err := paths.WorktreeRoot(context.Background())\n130\t\t\tif err == nil {\n131\t\t\t\trepoPath = root\n132\t\t\t} else {\n133\t\t\t\tlogging.Debug(context.Background(), \"pi: GetSessionDir falling back to cwd\",\n134\t\t\t\t\tslog.String(\"err\", err.Error()))\n135\t\t\t\t//nolint:forbidigo // last-resort fallback when no git repo (tests outside repos)\n136\t\t\t\twd, wdErr := os.Getwd()\n137\t\t\t\tif wdErr != nil {\n138\t\t\t\t\treturn \"\", fmt.Errorf(\"resolve repo root or cwd for pi session dir: %w\", wdErr)\n139\t\t\t\t}\n140\t\t\t\trepoPath = wd\n141\t\t\t}\n142\t\t}\n143\t\treturn filepath.Join(repoPath, paths.EntireTmpDir, piSessionSubdir), nil\n144\t}\n145\t\n146\t// ResolveSessionFile returns the full path to a captured Pi session JSONL\n147\t// file for the given session ID inside sessionDir.\n148\tfunc (a *PiAgent) ResolveSessionFile(sessionDir, agentSessionID string) string {\n149\t\treturn filepath.Join(sessionDir, agentSessionID+\".json\")\n150\t}\n151\t\n152\t// ReadSession loads a captured Pi transcript and returns it as an AgentSession.\n153\tfunc (a *PiAgent) ReadSession(input *agent.HookInput) (*agent.AgentSession, error) {\n154\t\tif input == nil || input.SessionRef == \"\" {\n155\t\t\treturn nil, errors.New(\"no session ref provided\")\n156\t\t}\n157\t\n158\t\tdata, err := os.ReadFile(input.SessionRef)\n159\t\tif err != nil {\n160\t\t\treturn nil, fmt.Errorf(\"read pi session: %w\", err)\n161\t\t}\n162\t\treturn &agent.AgentSession{\n163\t\t\tAgentName:  a.Name(),\n164\t\t\tSessionID:  input.SessionID,\n165\t\t\tSessionRef: input.SessionRef,\n166\t\t\tNativeData: data,\n167\t\t}, nil\n168\t}\n169\t\n170\t// WriteSession writes a captured Pi transcript back to disk so Pi can resume\n171\t// from it. Pi loads sessions from arbitrary paths via `pi --session <path>`,\n172\t// so a plain write is sufficient.\n173\tfunc (a *PiAgent) WriteSession(_ context.Context, session *agent.AgentSession) error {\n174\t\tif session == nil {\n175\t\t\treturn errors.New(\"nil session\")\n176\t\t}\n177\t\tif session.SessionRef == \"\" {\n178\t\t\treturn errors.New(\"session has empty SessionRef\")\n179\t\t}\n180\t\tif len(session.NativeData) == 0 {\n181\t\t\treturn errors.New(\"session has empty NativeData\")\n182\t\t}\n183\t\tif err := os.MkdirAll(filepath.Dir(session.SessionRef), 0o750); err != nil {\n184\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"create pi session dir: %w\", err)\n185\t\t}\n186\t\n187\t\tif err := os.WriteFile(session.SessionRef, session.NativeData, 0o600); err != nil {\n188\t\t\treturn fmt.Errorf(\"write pi session file: %w\", err)\n189\t\t}\n190\t\treturn nil\n191\t}\n192\t\n193\t// FormatResumeCommand returns the shell command to resume a specific Pi\n194\t// session by ID. Pi accepts a partial UUID via `pi --session <id>`. When no\n195\t// session is specified, fall back to `pi --continue` which reopens the most\n196\t// recent session.\n197\tfunc (a *PiAgent) FormatResumeCommand(sessionID string) string {\n198\t\tid := strings.TrimSpace(sessionID)\n199\t\tif id == \"\" {\n200\t\t\treturn \"pi --continue\"\n201\t\t}\n202\t\treturn \"pi --session \" + id\n203\t}"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"2e6facd9-dae1-4639-8e3f-13dd964bfcf5","timestamp":"2026-05-09T21:26:13.659Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"824c9ef4-e4d5-49d7-ad05-c34c07511466","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"soph/pi-cold-attach-and-e2e"}
{"parentUuid":"2e6facd9-dae1-4639-8e3f-13dd964bfcf5","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/cmd/entire/cli/config.go","snippet":"9\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/types\"\n10\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/settings\"\n11\t\t\"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/strategy\"\n12\t\n13\t\t// Import agents to register them\n14\t\t_ \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/claudecode\"\n15\t\t_ \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/codex\"\n16\t\t_ \"github.com/entireio/cli/cmd/entire/cli/agent/factoryaidroid\"\n17\t)\n18\t\n19\t// Package-level aliases to avoid shadowing the settings package with local variables named \"settings\".\n20\tconst (\n21\t\tEntireSettingsFile      = settings.EntireSettingsFile\n22\t\tEntireSettingsLocalFile = settings.EntireSettingsLocalFile\n23\t)\n24\t"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"93ab4107-1c3f-4e3f-bb61-0be47bc285f3","timestamp":"2026-05-09T21:26:13.659Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"824c9ef4-e4d5-49d7-ad05-c34c07511466","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"soph/pi-cold-attach-and-e2e"}
{"parentUuid":"93ab4107-1c3f-4e3f-bb61-0be47bc285f3","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli/CLAUDE.md","snippet":"1\t# Entire - CLI\n2\t\n3\tThis repo contains the CLI for Entire.\n4\t\n5\t## Architecture\n6\t\n7\t- CLI built with github.com/spf13/cobra and github.com/charmbracelet/huh\n8\t\n9\t## Key Directories\n10\t\n11\t### Commands (`cmd/`)\n12\t\n13\t- `entire/`: Main CLI entry point. Also home to kubectl-style external-command resolution (`entire <name>` → `entire-<name>` on PATH) — see [External Commands](docs/architecture/external-commands.md).\n14\t- `entire/cli`: CLI utilities and helpers (Cobra commands, helpers, group roots)\n15\t- `entire/cli/commands`: actual command implementations\n16\t- `entire/cli/agent`: agent implementations (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI) - see [Agent Integration Checklist](docs/architecture/agent-integration-checklist.md) and [Agent Implementation Guide](docs/architecture/agent-guide.md)\n17\t- `entire/cli/strategy`: strategy implementation (manual-commit) - see section below\n18\t- `entire/cli/checkpoint`: checkpoint storage abstractions (temporary and committed)\n19\t- `entire/cli/session`: session state management\n20\t- `entire/cli/integration_test`: integration tests (simulated hooks)\n21\t- `e2e/`: E2E tests with real agent calls (see [e2e/README.md](e2e/README.md))\n22\t\n23\t### Command Layout\n24\t\n25\tThe CLI is organized around five noun groups plus a small set of top-level\n26\tverbs. The groups are the canonical home for each verb; legacy top-level\n27\tshortcuts remain functional but hidden, and emit a deprecation hint pointing\n28\tat the canonical group form.\n29\t\n30\t- `session` (alias: `sessions`): `list`, `info`, `stop`, `attach`, `resume`, `current`\n31\t- `checkpoint` (aliases: `cp`, `checkpoints`): `list`, `explain`, `rewind`, `search`\n32\t- `agent`: bare opens the interactive agent selector, plus `list`, `add`, `remove`\n33\t- `configure`: bare prints help and a hint pointing at `entire agent`; flags\n34\t  manage non-agent settings (telemetry, git-hook installation mode, strategy\n35\t  options, summary provider). Agent CRUD lives under `entire agent`.\n36\t- `auth`: `login`, `logout`, `status`, `list`, `revoke`\n37\t- `doctor`: bare runs the scan-and-fix flow, plus `trace`, `logs`, `bundle`\n38\t\n39\tTop-level lifecycle and standalone commands: `enable`, `disable`, `status`,\n40\t`login`, `logout`, `clean`, `version`, `dispatch`, `activity`, `help`,\n41\t`configure`.\n42\t\n43\tHidden top-level shortcuts (functional, emit a one-line deprecation hint):\n44\t`rewind` → `checkpoint rewind`, `resume` → `session resume`, `attach` →\n45\t`session attach`, `explain` → `checkpoint explain`, `trace` → `doctor trace`.\n46\tCobra-native aliases (no hint): `sessions` → `session`, `cp`/`checkpoints` →\n47\t`checkpoint`. The `search` top-level remains hidden without a hint.\n48\t\n49\tDeprecated top-level alias (functional, prints cobra deprecation message):\n50\t`reset` → `clean`.\n51\t\n52\tHidden infrastructure commands: `hooks`, `migrate`, `trail`,\n53\t`curl-bash-post-install`, `__send_analytics`.\n54\t\n55\tThe `hideAsAlias(cmd, canonical)` helper in `cmd/entire/cli/aliascmd.go`\n56\tmarks a command Hidden and sets cobra's `Deprecated` field so the hint\n57\trenders to stderr on every invocation while the command stays functional.\n58\tDiagnostic subcommands live alongside `doctor.go` as `doctor_logs.go` and\n59\t`doctor_bundle.go`. Group roots and noun-group children live in files\n60\tnamed `<noun>_group.go` and `<noun>_<verb>.go` respectively.\n61\t\n62\t## Tech Stack\n63\t\n64\t- Language: Go 1.26.x\n65\t- Build tool: mise, go modules\n66\t- Linting: golangci-lint\n67\t\n68\t## Development\n69\t\n70\t### Running Tests\n71\t\n72\t```bash\n73\tmise run test\n74\t```\n75\t\n76\t### Running Integration Tests\n77\t\n78\t```bash\n79\tmise run test:integration\n80\t```\n81\t\n82\t### Running All Tests (CI)\n83\t\n84\t```bash\n85\tmise run test:ci\n86\t```\n87\t\n88\tThis runs unit tests, integration tests, and the E2E canary (Vogon agent) in sequence. Integration tests use the `//go:build integration` build tag and are located in `cmd/entire/cli/integration_test/`.\n89\t\n90\t### Running E2E Canary Tests (Vogon Agent)\n91\t\n92\tThe Vogon agent is a deterministic fake agent that exercises the full E2E test suite without making any API calls. Named after the Vogons from The Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy — bureaucratic, procedural, and deterministic to a fault.\n93\t\n94\t```bash\n95\tmise run test:e2e:canary           # Run all E2E tests with the Vogon agent\n96\tmise run test:e2e:canary TestFoo   # Run a specific test\n97\t```\n98\t\n99\t- **Runs as part of `test:ci`** — canary failures block merges\n100\t- **No API calls, no cost** — safe to run freely, unlike real agent E2E tests\n101\t- **If a canary test fails, the bug is in the CLI or test infrastructure**, not in an agent\n102\t- Located in `e2e/vogon/` (binary) and `cmd/entire/cli/agent/vogon/` (Agent interface)\n103\t- The binary parses prompts via regex, creates/modifies/deletes files, and fires lifecycle hooks\n104\t- **IMPORTANT: When changing E2E test prompt wording**, the Vogon binary (`e2e/vogon/main.go`) parses prompts with hardcoded regexes. New phrasing may not match existing patterns — always run `mise run test:e2e:canary` after changing prompt text and fix Vogon's parsing if tests fail.\n105\t\n106\t### Running E2E Tests (Only When Explicitly Requested)\n107\t\n108\t**IMPORTANT: Do NOT run E2E tests proactively.** E2E tests make real API calls to agents, which consume tokens and cost money. Only run them when the user explicitly asks for E2E testing.\n109\t\n110\t```bash\n111\tmise run test:e2e [filter]                          # All agents, filtered\n112\tmise run test:e2e --agent claude-code [filter]       # Claude Code only\n113\tmise run test:e2e --agent gemini-cli [filter]        # Gemini CLI only\n114\tmise run test:e2e --agent opencode [filter]          # OpenCode only\n115\tmise run test:e2e --agent cursor [filter]            # Cursor only\n116\tmise run test:e2e --agent factoryai-droid [filter]   # Factory AI Droid only\n117\tmise run test:e2e --agent copilot-cli [filter]       # Copilot CLI only\n118\t```\n119\t\n120\tE2E tests:\n121\t\n122\t- Use the `//go:build e2e` build tag\n123\t- Located in `e2e/tests/`\n124\t- See [`e2e/README.md`](e2e/README.md) for full documentation (structure, debugging, adding agents)\n125\t- Test real agent interactions (Claude Code, Gemini CLI, OpenCode, Cursor, Factory AI Droid, Copilot CLI, or Vogon creating files, committing, etc.)\n126\t- Validate checkpoint scenarios documented in `docs/architecture/checkpoint-scenarios.md`\n127\t- Support multiple agents via `E2E_AGENT` env var (`claude-code`, `gemini`, `opencode`, `cursor`, `factoryai-droid`, `copilot-cli`, `vogon`)\n128\t\n129\t**Environment variables:**\n130\t\n131\t- `E2E_AGENT` - Agent to test with (default: `claude-code`)\n132\t- `E2E_CLAUDE_MODEL` - Claude model to use (default: `haiku` for cost efficiency)\n133\t- `E2E_TIMEOUT` - Timeout per prompt (default: `2m`)\n134\t\n135\t### Test Parallelization\n136\t\n137\t**Always use `t.Parallel()` in tests.** Every top-level test function and subtest should call `t.Parallel()` unless it modifies process-global state (e.g., `os.Chdir()`).\n138\t\n139\t```go\n140\tfunc TestFeature_Foo(t *testing.T) {\n141\t    t.Parallel()\n142\t    // ...\n143\t}\n144\t\n145\t// Integration tests with TestEnv\n146\tfunc TestFeature_Bar(t *testing.T) {\n147\t    t.Parallel()\n148\t    env := NewFeatureBranchEnv(t)\n149\t    // ...\n150\t}\n151\t```\n152\t\n153\t**Exception:** Tests that modify process-global state cannot be parallelized. This includes `os.Chdir()`/`t.Chdir()` and `os.Setenv()`/`t.Setenv()` — Go's test framework will panic if these are used after `t.Parallel()`.\n154\t\n155\t### Git in Tests\n156\t\n157\t**Tests that touch git state must use an isolated temp repo — never the real repo CWD.**\n158\t\n159\tMany handlers (lifecycle, strategy, hooks) resolve the git repo from CWD via `OpenRepository`, `GetGitCommonDir`, `DetectFileChanges`, etc. Without isolation, tests can create session state files, shadow branches, or other artifacts in the real `.git/` directory.\n160\t\n161\tUse the `testutil` helpers:\n162\t\n163\t```go\n164\ttmpDir := t.TempDir()\n165\ttestutil.InitRepo(t, tmpDir)                    // git init + user config + disable GPG\n166\ttestutil.WriteFile(t, tmpDir, \"f.txt\", \"init\")  // create a file\n\n... [682 lines truncated] ..."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"a9c2b76b-96c2-4de6-a418-620711823c5e","timestamp":"2026-05-09T21:26:13.659Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"824c9ef4-e4d5-49d7-ad05-c34c07511466","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"soph/pi-cold-attach-and-e2e"}
