{"parentUuid":"d9801bba-5136-4371-820a-ffd6df54cddd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_015MLUue3sm2PqBUFB5xaSmn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01AnbS7gy5n5ZMf7tu97rorE","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"gh pr create --base feat/pi-agent-builtin --head soph/pi-cold-attach-and-e2e --title \"Pi: cold-attach native-store resolution, race fix, E2E coverage\" --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nStacks on top of #1170. Three substantive changes plus docs:\n\n## 1. `Resolve Pi sessions from native store` — cold attach\n\n`GetSessionDir` / `ResolveSessionFile` previously returned the per-repo `.entire/tmp/pi/` cache, which is only populated after `agent_end` copies the live JSONL there. `entire session attach <id>` for a Pi session that was never hooked (or whose hook capture failed) couldn't find the transcript at all — defeating attach's documented \"hooks failed / weren't installed\" recovery use case.\n\nMove resolution to Pi's native store at `<piHome>/sessions/<encoded-repo-path>/<timestamp>_<id>.jsonl`, with the encoded path matching Pi's own naming scheme (`/Users/foo/repo` → `--Users-foo-repo--`). Honor `PI_CODING_AGENT_DIR` (Pi's own override) and add `ENTIRE_TEST_PI_SESSION_DIR` for test isolation. Add `GetSessionBaseDir` so attach's cross-project fallback (`searchTranscriptInProjectDirs`) can scan sibling project subdirs.\n\n`ResolveSessionFile` now globs `*_<id>.jsonl` and returns the most recent timestamp match; absolute paths from hook payloads still pass through unchanged. The `.entire/tmp/pi/` cache stays as a hook-internal detail — the renamed `piHookCacheSubdir` constant lives in `lifecycle.go` to make the agent-public-API vs hook-internal split obvious.\n\n**Trade-off:** `AgentForTranscriptPath` ownership matching now matches live Pi paths and misses cached paths, instead of the inverse. Cached paths are only reachable via Pi's own hook flow, where caller-agent-type fallback already resolves ownership correctly; live-path matching is the more important case because that's the one cold attach surfaces.\n\n## 2. `Drop SessionEnd from pi session_shutdown hook` — race fix\n\nSurfaced by the new e2e suite. The TS extension fires `agent_end` and `session_shutdown` async via separate `execFile` child processes; they race in Node's event loop. When `session_shutdown` wins, the emitted `SessionEnd` transitions the session to `ended` and condenses it before `agent_end` can save its linkable checkpoint. `prepare-commit-msg` then sees a \"fully-condensed ended session\" and the user's commit gets no checkpoint trailer.\n\nReproduced reliably on `TestSingleSessionManualCommit/pi`:\n- Before: 37.7s timeout failure (\"checkpoint ref entire/checkpoints/v1 did not advance within 30s\")\n- After: 8.5s pass\n\nFix: `session_shutdown` is cleanup-only — clears the cached session ID, emits no lifecycle event. `agent_end` is the source of truth for \"turn complete\" (and effectively \"session over\" for any single-turn `pi -p` invocation). `SessionEnd` is left for the framework to derive from idle timeout or the next `SessionStart`'s stale-state cleanup.\n\n## 3. `Add Pi to the E2E agent registry` — coverage\n\n`e2e/agents/pi.go` registers Pi via `E2E_AGENT=pi`. #1170's canary used Vogon, not pi — so the hooked flow had no integration coverage at all. This adapter is what surfaced the race in #2.\n\n## 4. `Document Pi in CLAUDE.md`\n\nAgent enumeration + per-agent test:e2e flag table + e2e agent enumeration + `E2E_AGENT` env var values.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `mise run lint` — 0 issues\n- `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/pi/...` — all pass (40+ tests + 9 new for cold-attach)\n- Cold attach against an unhooked pi session: resolves live JSONL in `~/.pi/agent/sessions/`, produces valid `Entire-Checkpoint` trailer, parses token usage correctly\n- `TestSingleSessionManualCommit/pi` passes in 8.5s with race fix (was failing 37.7s without)\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [ ] CI green\n- [ ] `mise run test:e2e --agent pi TestSingleSessionManualCommit` passes against a fresh Pi install\n- [ ] Manual cold-attach: `pi -p \"hello\"` in an un-`enable`d repo, then `entire session attach --agent pi <id>` — expect a valid checkpoint trailer\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -5","description":"Open PR targeting feat/pi-agent-builtin"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":467,"cache_read_input_tokens":489774,"output_tokens":1809,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":467,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1809,"cache_read_input_tokens":489774,"cache_creation_input_tokens":467,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":467},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CasjjSN1boCWL1fE9DPrD","type":"assistant","uuid":"1b4faf30-1aaa-43ca-b9ec-21d6ce4d65a1","timestamp":"2026-05-09T21:53:40.042Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/soph/Work/entire/devenv/cli","sessionId":"824c9ef4-e4d5-49d7-ad05-c34c07511466","version":"2.1.136","gitBranch":"soph/pi-cold-attach-and-e2e"}
